# List filter panel

Use `@webonone/ui-kit` **`ListFilterTrigger`** and **`ListFilterPanel`** on any `FeaturePage` that displays a filterable collection (`ItemList` + `Pagination`).

Skill: [.cursor/skills/item-list/SKILL.md](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) · pagination: [item-list-pagination.mdc](item-list-pagination.mdc).

Reference: `ui-kit/package/src/components/ListFilterPanel.tsx`, `email/frontend/src/features/history/pages/HistoryPage.tsx`.

## When required

- Page shows a paginated or slice-paginated **collection list**
- User can narrow results by status, date, search text, or similar criteria

## Pattern

```tsx
<FeaturePage
  title="…"
  actions={<ListFilterTrigger active={hasActiveFilters} onClick={() => setFilterOpen(true)} />}
>
  <ListFilterPanel
    open={filterOpen}
    onOpenChange={setFilterOpen}
    onApply={handleApply}
    onClear={handleClear}
  >
    {/* FormField + Select / Input / DatePicker */}
  </ListFilterPanel>
  <ItemList>…</ItemList>
  <Pagination … />
</FeaturePage>
```

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| No inline filter forms | Do not add full-width `<Form>` rows above lists — use the panel |
| `active` trigger | `true` when any filter ≠ default (e.g. status not `all`, search non-empty) |
| Apply | Reset pagination to page 1; refetch (server) or re-slice (client) |
| Clear | Reset filter state to defaults and refresh list |

## Exceptions

- Auth, embed, and form-only pages (no collection list)
- Single-card pages (e.g. Providers)
- Media embed routes (`/picker`, `/upload`) — filter in `ScopedFolderBrowser` toolbar when list is shown

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w <service-root>
```
